Title:
Sliver C2 Evasion Suite

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This repository provides a modular “evasion suite” for the Sliver C2 framework, aiming to replicate common Cobalt Strike tradecraft for stealthy execution and staging. It includes four kits: an in-memory execution extension (Loader Kit), two sleep-masking implementations (Sleep Mask Kit), a Go reimplementation of the closed-source Crystal Palace COFF-to-PIC linker plus operator workflow (Crystal Palace Kit), and a process injection toolkit with PPID spoofing (Inject Kit). Core techniques include PIC shellcode with no PE headers/IAT, ROR13 PEB-walk API resolution, staged payload delivery via one-shot self-signed HTTPS, and consistent avoidance of RWX memory. The suite also covers practical bypass primitives such as AMSI/WLDP patching (via Donut in Loader Kit) and AMSI/ETW patching plus basic anti-sandbox checks (standalone InjectKit EXE). It’s primarily useful for red teams/pentesters operating Sliver who want more evasive staging, execution, and injection workflows, and for defenders/researchers studying modern implant hardening patterns in open source. The most notable component is PalaceKit, which implements Crystal Palace-style spec/DSL linking, relocations, and DFR attach/preserve mechanics to produce loader shellcode without relying on the proprietary Java tool.

Technical Focus:
- Sliver C2 extensions and operator-side staging workflows (Go + C)
- PIC shellcode generation: COFF linking, relocation handling (REL32/ADDR64), +gofirst rotation
- DFR (Dynamic Function Resolution) with attach/preserve rewriting and PEB-walk API resolution (ROR13 hashing)
- Sleep masking via inline hooks (NtWaitForSingleObject / kernel32!Sleep), memory encryption, and RX/RW toggling
- NT-native injection chain (NtAllocateVirtualMemory/NtWriteVirtualMemory/NtCreateThreadEx) and PPID spoofing
- Staged payload crypto and delivery (XOR layers, ChaCha20/ChaCha20-Poly1305, one-shot HTTPS)

Use Cases:
- Run .NET assemblies and native tools in-memory from an active Sliver session with output capture (execute-assembly analogue)
- Reduce memory-scan exposure during beacon sleep by encrypting shellcode and removing execute permissions
- Build Crystal Palace-style loaders (no IAT/PE headers) for Sliver shellcode without proprietary tooling
- Stage and inject Sliver shellcode into benign host processes, including spawn+inject with PPID spoofing
- Chain components (e.g., Sliver shellcode → sleep masker → PIC loader → injector) for layered evasion

Keywords:
Sliver, C2, defense evasion, in-memory execution, Donut, execute-assembly, sleep mask, NtWaitForSingleObject, kernel32!Sleep hook, stack spoofing, ROR13 hashing, PEB walk, dynamic API resolution, COFF linker, relocations, position-independent code, NtAllocateVirtualMemory, NtProtectVirtualMemory, NtCreateThreadEx, PPID spoofing, PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS, AMSI, WLDP, ETW patching, ChaCha20-Poly1305, WinHTTP, one-shot HTTPS staging